WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.739
Mass assignment, also called over-posting, happens when request data is
allowed to populate model fields more broadly than intended.

2
00:00:07.739 --> 00:00:16.428
A client may submit fields such as role, owner, tenant, price, status,
approval flag, or audit metadata that should be controlled by server-side
logic.

3
00:00:16.428 --> 00:00:24.711
If create or update paths blindly copy request dictionaries into model
instances, the application can lose control over sensitive attributes.

4
00:00:24.711 --> 00:00:29.259
The safest create and update paths use explicit allowlists of writable
fields.

5
00:00:29.259 --> 00:00:38.899
Read-only fields, derived fields, ownership fields, workflow fields, and
administrative fields should be set by trusted server-side logic rather
than client input.

6
00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:42.089
Different actions may have different writable fields.

7
00:00:42.089 --> 00:00:51.458
A profile update, admin edit, account recovery flow, and import job should
not automatically share the same field permissions just because they use
the same model.

8
00:00:51.458 --> 00:00:56.413
Serialization can expose sensitive data when it mirrors model structure
too closely.

9
00:00:56.413 --> 00:01:04.831
Generic serializers, debug views, nested relationships, and automatic API
responses may return fields the caller does not need or should not see.

10
00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:07.479
Response minimization is a security control.

11
00:01:07.479 --> 00:01:15.218
Serializers should be designed around use cases, caller permissions, and
audience, not only around what fields exist in the database.

12
00:01:15.218 --> 00:01:18.137
Nested relationships deserve special attention.

13
00:01:18.137 --> 00:01:27.709
Returning a project may accidentally include owner details, billing
records, tokens, internal notes, or cross-tenant relationships if
serialization is too broad.

14
00:01:27.709 --> 00:01:32.597
Create, update, and serialize paths should be intentionally designed and
reviewed.

15
00:01:32.597 --> 00:01:34.905
The ORM model is not the public contract.

16
00:01:34.905 --> 00:01:40.200
It is an internal representation that must be mediated before data crosses
a trust boundary.
